{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118873","id":3571031196,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7U2Zyc","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118873","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118873.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118873.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118873","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118873/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118873/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118873/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/d47fcea6ab7354239b2bbebcef556014600297f9","number":118873,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Rewrite HashMap and AHashMap around SwissTable probing","user":{"login":"dsh0416","id":2303500,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDM1MDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2303500?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsh0416","html_url":"https://github.com/dsh0416","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsh0416/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsh0416/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsh0416/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsh0416/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsh0416/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsh0416/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsh0416/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsh0416/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsh0416/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Motivation\r\n\r\nHashMaps are everywhere in Godot, no matter in the engine or the game logics. The Swiss-table family of designs (Abseil [flat_hash_map](https://abseil.io/blog/20180927-swisstables), Rust [hashbrown](https://github.com/rust-lang/hashbrown)) addresses with a 1-byte-per-slot control array that lets a single SIMD/SWAR comparison reject or short-list 8 slots at once. We borrow that idea to improve the performance of Godot's hashmap. We adopted SwissTable as the probing/index mechanism, but we bent the storage layer around Godot’s stronger API guarantees and existing container behavior.\r\n\r\n## What changed\r\n- rewrite `HashMap` and `AHashMap` to use a SwissTable-style control-byte index with SIMD-scanned probe groups\r\n- preserve `HashMap`'s insertion-order iteration and live-entry pointer stability while keeping `AHashMap` dense and swap-on-erase\r\n- introduce cached full hashes, SIMD erase tombstone handling, foldhash-based string hashing, a stable-handle ordered arena, and a metadata/payload split for ordered entries\r\n- add focused tests and benchmarks for `HashMap`, `AHashMap`, SwissTable SIMD helpers, and `Dictionary` order/hash behavior\r\n- compact ordered HashMap index and metadata, learned from Ruby's [patch 1](https://bugs.ruby-lang.org/issues/22011) and [patch 2](https://bugs.ruby-lang.org/issues/12142).\r\n\r\n## Benchmark (running on Macbook Pro M4)\r\n\r\n\r\nWorkload | Legacy | New | Delta | Change\r\n-- | -- | -- | -- | --\r\nHashMap<int,int> insert | 47.7 | 24.1 | -23.6 | -49.5%\r\nHashMap<int,int> lookup-hit | 7.3 | 4.5 | -2.8 | -38.4%\r\nHashMap<int,int> lookup-miss | 11.3 | 8.0 | -3.3 | -29.2%\r\nHashMap<int,int> erase | 27.3 | 17.6 | -9.7 | -35.5%\r\nAHashMap<int,int> insert | 31.2 | 8.1 | -23.1 | -74.0%\r\nAHashMap<int,int> lookup-hit | 4.9 | 3.1 | -1.8 | -36.7%\r\nAHashMap<int,int> erase | 11.5 | 13.8 | +2.3 | +20.0%\r\nAHashMap<int,int> churn | 8.5 | 8.5 | +0.0 | +0.0%\r\nHashMap<String,int> insert | 54.3 | 28.9 | -25.4 | -46.8%\r\nHashMap<String,int> lookup-hit | 12.5 | 10.0 | -2.5 | -20.0%\r\nHashMap<String,int> erase | 26.6 | 24.7 | -1.9 | -7.1%\r\nHashMap<StringName,Variant> insert | 82.8 | 26.5 | -56.3 | -68.0%\r\nHashMap<StringName,Variant> lookup-hit | 7.5 | 6.0 | -1.5 | -20.0%\r\nHashMap<StringName,Variant> erase | 19.3 | 17.8 | -1.5 | -7.8%\r\n\r\n\r\n## Notes\r\n\r\nTests and docs are written by AI, some of the code are rewritten by AI with some of my proven working code in Rust.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-04-23T04:35:52Z","updated_at":"2026-04-23T06:40:48Z","closed_at":"2026-04-23T06:40:28Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"d3f8b27c6f86736d91de121e1c33749f3f5c37a8","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"dsh0416:dsh0416/swiss","ref":"dsh0416/swiss","repo":{"id":646512981,"node_id":"R_kgDOJokBVQ","name":"godot","full_name":"dsh0416/godot","owner":{"login":"dsh0416","id":2303500,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDM1MDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2303500?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsh0416","html_url":"https://github.com/dsh0416","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsh0416/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsh0416/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsh0416/gis